# Text files are checked out with LF everywhere: the vendored scripts carry Subresource Integrity hashes
# (web/index.html), and a CRLF checkout on Windows changes their bytes so the browser refuses them.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.stl binary
*.3mf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.wasm binary
*.dcm binary
